    "result_text": "All green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole test class (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` case) passes.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe codebase already has a per-city cap enforced by `CityCapacity.isFull` (rejects at 50), and a parallel \"flag stored at creation, surfaced in the response\" pattern for `bulkSignupWarning`. I followed that exact convention, keeping every touched function trivial:\n\n1. **`CityCapacity.java`** \u2014 added `WARN_THRESHOLD = 40` and a new `isApproaching(...)` method (true when the city holds 40\u201349). Extracted the shared `count(...)` helper so `isFull` and `isApproaching` share one line of counting logic; the hard rejection at 50 is unchanged.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean capacityWarning` field with a plain getter/setter (CC 1 each), mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`.\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one line: `owner.setCapacityWarning(CityCapacity.isApproaching(owners, owner));`, next to the existing `setBulkSignupWarning`.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property to the Owner schema, so the generated DTO carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it (same-named field, no explicit `@Mapping` needed).\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\n- The only change to a function in a large class is the single trivial line in `addOwner` (no new branches, so its CC is unchanged).\n- The real logic lives in the tiny `CityCapacity` class (WMC of the rest of the class \u2248 1), and the new/changed functions are all CC 1\u20132.\n- No existing behavior changed; the 50-owner hard reject is untouched.",
